# Graduate Econometrics
#
# The estimator matrix of the graduate sequence: likelihood, moments, structural and reduced-form models, and time series, each beside the assumption it leans on and the test that checks it.

#>economics_grad_econometrics
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!economics
#:form #!comparison
#:level #!graduate
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!bone

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Graduate Econometrics"
 ~#claim: "Each graduate estimator trades an assumption for a property, so the matrix pairs likelihood, moments, structural models, and time series with the test that catches the broken assumption."
 ~#proof: "Rows cite Fisher, Haavelmo, Sargan, Hansen, White, Newey and West, Heckman, Hausman, Sims, Engle and Granger, Johansen, Rust, and Berry, Levinsohn, and Pakes."
 ~#door: "Pick an estimator, read its broken-assumption cell, run the random-walk kit, then read the structural debate."
 ~#audience: "graduate students and applied researchers choosing an estimator"
 continuity: "Graduate Econometrics | broken assumption"
 cold_open: "Every estimator leans on one assumption, and each row here names the test that catches the broken assumption."
}

